<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malolos Constitution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1899</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Political Constitution of 1899</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malolos">Malolos</a> Constitution was the constitution of the First Philippine Republic, drafted by a revolutionary congress at Barasoain church in Malolos, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulacan">Bulacan</a>, from September 1898 and promulgated in January 1899. Drawing on Spanish and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> American models, it created a republic with a strong legislature. It was the first republican constitution in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>, though the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war">Philippine–American War</a> soon ended the republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malolos-constitution.jpg" alt="Malolos Constitution" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author or not provided · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:General_Aguinaldo_(seated,_center)_and_ten_of_the_delegates_to_the_first_Assembly_of_Representatives_that_passed_the_Con_-_NARA_-_530993.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
